# Line endings.
#
# This matters more than usual here. cmd.exe is mostly tolerant of LF-only
# batch files, but not reliably so around labels and `goto` -- a .cmd file with
# Unix endings can fail in ways that look like a logic bug rather than a
# whitespace problem. diskpart is fussier still about its script files. So both
# are pinned to CRLF regardless of what platform the working copy is on.
#
# C sources and Markdown stay LF: every compiler and editor in play handles
# them, and it keeps diffs clean when the repo is touched from Linux.

* text=auto

*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.txt  text eol=crlf

*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
Makefile*  text eol=lf

*.exe  binary
*.wim  binary
